charts if extra metadata/path is passed**\\n4. The pipeline rule says not to modify `/tmp/crypto-article.md`, but then **nothing downstream actually replaces the placeholders**\\n\\n### Clean problem statement for your system fix\\n**Problem:** The pipeline successfully generates `/tmp/chart.png`, but the article markdown still contains raw `[CHART_PLACEHOLDER]` tokens when passed to WordPress publishing. The wp-publisher stage is not converting those placeholders into actual embedded chart images, so the final draft post has no chart images.\\n\\n### Evidence\\n- `/tmp/chart.png` present\\n- `/tmp/crypto-article.md` still has 2 placeholder tokens\\n- published draft URL resolves incorrectly / doesn’t expose embedded chart output as expected\\n\\nIf you want, I can next give you a **very precise fix spec** for the wp-publisher handoff only, without changing anything myself.\"},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"I’m checking the draft and the source article now so I can tell you exactly where the chart handoff broke.\"},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Yep — you’re right. The chart placeholders are still in the article, and the live draft isn’t showing chart images.\\n\\n### What broke\\n- `/tmp/chart.png` **does exist**\\n- `/tmp/crypto-article.md` still contains:\\n  - line 23: `[CHART_PLACEHOLDER]`\\n  - line 47: `[CHART_PLACEHOLDER]`\\n\\n### Real issue\\nThe **chart was generated**, but it was **never injected into the article/publish flow in a way WordPress actually used**.\\n\\nThat means the failure is in the **handoff between chart generation and wp-publisher**, not in chart creation itself.\\n\\n### Likely pipeline fault\\nOne of these is true:\\n1. **wp-publisher expects a different placeholder format**\\n2. **wp-publisher is not processing `[CHART_PLACEHOLDER]` markers at all**\\n3. **wp-publisher only knows how to insert charts if extra metadata/path is passed**\\n4. The pipeline rule says not to modify `/tmp/crypto-article.md`, but then **nothing downstream actually replaces the placeholders**\\n\\n### Clean problem statement for your system fix\\n**Problem:** The pipeline successfully generates `/tmp/chart.png`, but the article markdown still contains raw `[CHART_PLACEHOLDER]` tokens when passed to WordPress publishing. The wp-publisher stage is not converting those placeholders into actual embedded chart images, so the final draft post has no chart images.\\n\\n### Evidence\\n- `/tmp/chart.png` present\\n- `/tmp/crypto-article.md` still has 2 placeholder tokens\\n- published draft URL resolves incorrectly / doesn’t expose embedded chart output as expected\\n\\nIf you want, I can next give you a **very precise fix spec** for the wp-publisher handoff only, without changing anything myself.\"}],\"api\":\"openai-completions\",\"provider\":\"local-bifrost\",\"model\":\"gpt-5.4\",\"usage\":{\"input\":0,\"output\":0,\"cacheRead\":0,\"cacheWrite\":0,\"totalTokens\":0,\"cost\":{\"input\":0,\"output\":0,\"cacheRead\":0,\"cacheWrite\":0,\"total\":0}},\"stopReason\":\"stop\",\"timestamp\":1779092478679,\"responseId\":\"chatcmpl-DgnVy88KuJO8u8lQoZ8waJ4KLK6C8\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"System (untrusted): [2026-05-18 08:20:57 UTC] Exec completed (vivid-ze, code 0) :: https://slateblue-reindeer-775070.hostingersite.com/?p=91\\n\\nConversation info (untrusted metadata):\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"chat_id\\\": \\\"telegram:5691449303\\\",\\n  \\\"message_id\\\": \\\"356\\\",\\n  \\\"reply_to_id\\\": \\\"355\\\",\\n  \\\"sender_id\\\": \\\"5691449303\\\",\\n  \\\"sender\\\": \\\"Sawan bhardwaj\\\",\\n  \\\"timestamp\\\": \\\"Mon 2026-05-18 08:21 UTC\\\",\\n  \\\"has_reply_context\\\": true\\n}\\n```\\n\\nSender (untrusted metadata):\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"label\\\": \\\"Sawan bhardwaj (5691449303)\\\",\\n  \\\"id\\\": \\\"5691449303\\\",\\n  \\\"name\\\": \\\"Sawan bhardwaj\\\",\\n  \\\"username\\\": \\\"hero_fr_fun\\\"\\n}\\n```\\n\\nReplied message (untrusted, for context):\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"sender_l