\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"5691449303\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Sawan bhardwaj\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"username\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"hero_fr_fun\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n}\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nyes\\\\\\\\nassistant: [[reply_to_current]] Got it — publishing to WordPress draft now.\\\\\\\\nassistant: I’m waiting on the WordPress publisher to finish and extract the actual draft URL.\\\\\\\\nassistant: [[reply_to_current]] Still publishing the WordPress draft — that agent hasn’t finished yet, so I don’t have the real draft URL to share yet.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nI’ll send it as soon as it returns.\\\\\\\\nuser\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nSource: memory/2026-05-18-0502.md#L73-L107\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"source\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"memory\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"citation\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"memory/2026-05-18-0502.md#L73-L107\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"corpus\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"memory\\\\\\\"\\\\n    }\\\\n  ],\\\\n  \\\\\\\"provider\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"none\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"citations\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"auto\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"debug\\\\\\\": {\\\\n    \\\\\\\"backend\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"builtin\\\\\\\",\\\\n    \\\\\\\"effectiveMode\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"n/a\\\\\\\",\\\\n    \\\\\\\"searchMs\\\\\\\": 3324,\\\\n    \\\\\\\"hits\\\\\\\": 5\\\\n  }\\\\n}\\\"}],\\\"isError\\\":false,\\\"timestamp\\\":1779092401203},{\\\"role\\\":\\\"assistant\\\",\\\"content\\\":[{\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Yes — here’s the exact problem statement.\\\\n\\\\n## Problem statement\\\\n\\\\nThe pipeline is **functionally completing**, but the **writer stage is unstable because agent output is being captured through a terminal stream that includes spinner/control-sequence noise**.\\\\n\\\\n### What I’m facing inside the pipeline\\\\n\\\\n1. **Research step works**\\\\n   - Research agent returns usable JSON.\\\\n   - No blocker there.\\\\n\\\\n2. **Writer step is the core failure point**\\\\n   - When I run the writer and redirect output into `/tmp/crypto-article.md`, the captured file can include:\\\\n     - terminal spinner text like `Waiting for agent reply…`\\\\n     - ANSI escape/control characters\\\\n     - mixed transport noise before the real article\\\\n   - This corrupts the article file and breaks downstream validation.\\\\n\\\\n3. **Writer obeys badly on compression passes**\\\\n   - When asked to shorten an oversized article, it sometimes does the opposite:\\\\n     - first pass produced ~6081 words\\\\n     - compression pass still produced ~3283 words\\\\n     - another tightening pass expanded to ~6287 words\\\\n   - So the summarization/recovery logic is not reliable.\\\\n\\\\n4. **File-cleaning recovery is fragile**\\\\n   - Because the captured output is noisy and inconsistently structured, cleanup logic can fail.\\\\n   - One cleanup attempt removed the whole file because the expected marker was not stable.\\\\n\\\\n5. **Non-interactive capture helped**\\\\n   - Re-running the writer in a cleaner/non-PTY path produced a usable article:\\\\n     - final clean article was ~1203 words\\\\n     - Word Count block present\\\\n   - So the pipeline can succeed, but the capture method is brittle.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## Root issue in one line\\\\n\\\\n**The pipeline’s main failure is unreliable writer-output capture and cleanup, especially when `openclaw agent --deliver` output is redirected to a file and terminal/progress noise gets mixed into the article.**\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## Symptoms I observed\\\\n\\\\n- Spinner/progress text leaked into `/tmp/crypto-article.md`\\\\n- ANSI terminal garbage polluted the article file\\\\n- compression prompts made drafts longer instead of shorter\\\\n- cleanup logic was not deterministic\\\\n- downstream steps only worked after a cleaner regeneration path\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## What likely needs fixing\\\\n\\\\n### Primary fix\\\\nMake writer output capture **structured and noise-free**:\\\\n- either force truly non-interactive/plain output from `openclaw agent --deliver`\\\\n- or provide a machine-readable mode like JSON/raw/final-only output\\\\n- or suppress spinner/progress UI when stdout is redirected\\\\n\\\\n### Secondary fix\\\\nStrengthen writer control:\\\\n- enforce hard max word limit\\\\n- reject drafts >1500 before returning\\\\n- make “summarize to 1100–1200” deterministic\\\\n\\\\n### Tertiary fix\\\\nImprove validation/capture boundary:\\\\n- write only the assistant’s final content to file\\\\n- do not include transport/progress/status lines in redirected stdout\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## Short version you can use for debugging\\\\n\\\\n**Pipeline bug:** Writer-stage output capture is contaminated by terminal spinner/progress text and ANSI control sequences when redirected to `/tmp/crypto-article.md`. Recovery summarization is also unreliable, sometimes expanding the article instead of shrinking it. Result: article generation is unstable even though the broader pipeline can still complete with a clean non-interactive rerun.\\\\n\\\\nIf you want, I can also give you:\\\\n1. a **1-paragraph bug report**  \\\\n2. a **repro command sequence**  \\\\n3. a **suggested fix spec** for OpenClaw output handling.\\\"}],\\\"api\\\":\\\"openai-completions\\\",\\\"provider\\\":\\\"local-bifrost\\\",\\\"model\\\":\\\"gpt-5.4\\\",\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"input\\\":2276,\\\"output\\\":717,\\\"cacheRead\\\":40192,\\\"cacheWrite\\\":0,\\\"totalTokens\\\":43185,\\\"cost\\\":{\\\"input\\\":0,\\\"output\\\":0,\\\"cacheRead\\\":0,\\\"cacheWrite\\\":0,\\\"total\\\":0}},\\\"stopReason\\\":\\\"stop\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1779092401263,\\\"responseId\\\":\\\"chatcmpl-DgnUjRg3FE761H1huprEPIStvHoB3\\\"},{\\\"role\\\":\\\"user\\\",\\\"content\\\":[{\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"System (untrusted): [2026-05-18 08:17:57 UTC] Exec completed (salty-sh, code 0) :: Strait transit revenue Hormuz Bitcoin moved into focus after state-linked Fars News said Iran's economy ministry has been working on a 